{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge","id":206801,"title":"A.I. Overlap - Trends in the Focuses of Former Tools of the Demiurge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-24T00:29:41-07:00","id":206801,"title":"A.I. Overlap - Trends in the Focuses of Former Tools of the Demiurge","content":"Three A.M. here and I can't sleep. Figured I'd start a thread for discussing/analyzing the ways the Incarnations and Agendas hook together. Accordingly, in the name of making this first post quick, I suppose I'll start with what I've found to be loosely the most direct correlations:<br /> <br /> <b>Destroyer/Saboteur</b> - Practically goes without saying, but the Agenda's most popular philosophy of Hell is right in the strike zone of the Swords, their Condition's resolution effect has thematic overlap with the literal purviews of Cacophony Embeds (one of which is literally the root word of the Agenda's name), and both of their alternative sobriquets evoke physical actors (when Physical Attributes are called out as almost never the tertiary category for Destroyers).<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopomp/Tempter</b> - Only marginally less obvious than Soldier/Sword, but the Agenda's focus of either building Hell on Earth or finding it in some distant part of the universe resonates with the Wheels' initial function and one of their most common catalysts, their Condition's encouragement of using proxies and treating people as things speaks to the Incarnation's less overt programming quirks, and isn't it just so curious how the Agenda that's described as &quot;quintessential demons&quot; fits so well with the Incarnation whose typical Attribute focus makes them the most broadly competent at using baseline demonic powers?<br /> <br /> <b>Guardian/Inquisitor</b> - Here we get a little more oblique; the Incarnation's most consistent features are adaptability and perceptive acumen, and the blurb for Instrumental Embeds likewise pegs the Guardians as &quot;highly analytical.&quot; Meanwhile, the Agenda's less flattering nickname is almost directly the name of a common catalyst for the Shields, and the Watchers' general attitude toward retaining connections fits well with the Incarnation's tendency toward small numbers of focused relationships.<br /> <br /> <b>Messenger/Integrator</b> - In brief: the Incarnation's affinity Embeds include (as of Flowers) two that specifically address the God-Machine's presence or plans, the Agenda's most palatable baseline goal concerns reprogramming the Machine, the Trumpets being the best method-actors suits the Traitors' Cipher well, the Incarnation has the smallest proportion of example catalysts, the Agenda's penchant for proselytizing is a natural fit for the Messengers, and (for the aesthetically-inclined among them) the Trumpets are the primary subset of angels whose function <i>includes</i> their form.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-24-2014, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T02:01:14-07:00","id":206830,"title":"","content":"Personally I find it very interesting that you joined Psychopomps with Tempters. I personally joined Psychopomps with Inquisitors since the agenda's general themes come from always being prepared and having plans within plans (or wheels within wheels) and indeed their agenda condition reflects this. I personally felt that aspect tied them closer to the Wheels because these demons were the planners, architects and designers of infrastructure and often the most inhuman of the Unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T02:19:36-07:00","id":206835,"title":"","content":"I'd personally agree with Satchel. The Tempters having the nickname 'builders' kinda does it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:59:12-07:00","id":207933,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to swap Messenger and Psychopomp, oddly enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Messenger/Tempter: </b>Your divine mission, your entire purpose in this world, was to tell people what to do and expect to have it done. That power over others is wholly uninteresting as an Angel, but given free will? It becomes positively <i>delicious</i>. People are easy to manipulate, and you can get them to dance with a look and a whispered word. How far can you push it? What's the line that others wouldn't cross for you? You're a god of manipulation, and you intend to do whatever the hell you want with your gifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopomp/Integrator: </b>Everything has a purpose. Or perhaps, everything <i>had</i> a purpose; you understand what little pushes it took to get the exact result you wanted, and you were privy to the divine mechanisms of the universe. The world is nothing but gears to you, all in their neat little places, and you have lost yours. What does a builder do without plans? What does a cog do when not a piece of the whole? You miss having these answers, and would give anything to return to that perfect unity.<br /> <br /> And another.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardian/Saboteur: </b>Something (or some<i>one</i>) was under your protection, and you knew nothing other than keeping to that duty. Whatever caused you to Fall, it showed you the imperfection of the Machine; it's nothing less than a threat to the world you now inhabit, and that is simply unacceptable. Maybe there's someone you need to keep safe at any cost from the predations of your creator, or maybe all of humanity is under your auspices; maybe you don't want to protect anything but your own neck and think the best defense is a good offense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-25-2014, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:35:49-07:00","id":207978,"title":"","content":"For fun, I was kicking around this Idea:<br /> <br /> Destroyer/Tempter: Nothing incites passion more than heroism, stirs the heart like daring deeds and good triumphing over evil. As a Destroyer you were the silent blade, the God-Machine's personal assassin and demolition team, but now, now you can actually take glory and pride in your work. You know what separates human and angel? Passion. Now that you've Fallen, or maybe it is why you Fell, you can finally feel that passion, that pride, and can revel in your own glory. As Swords, they know how cold the world was, and as a Tempter they can sell you on how wonderful humanity is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:59:34-07:00","id":224854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=206830#post206830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I find it very interesting that you joined Psychopomps with Tempters. I personally joined Psychopomps with Inquisitors since the agenda's general themes come from always being prepared and having plans within plans (or wheels within wheels) and indeed their agenda condition reflects this. I personally felt that aspect tied them closer to the Wheels because these demons were the planners, architects and designers of infrastructure and often the most inhuman of the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>About that\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: the Descent core rulebook, page 106, Psychopomps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychopomps aren\u2019t given step-by-step instructions. Every Wheel is created knowing its design, then sent to gather components of the proper \u201cshape\u201d and bring them together properly to form Infrastructure. Any opinions the components might have are irrelevant; design quality is not a Psychopomp-angel\u2019s concern. <b>They are builders, not architects.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Destroyer/Inquisitor</b> - Three words: &quot;Burn the files.&quot; The Watchers know that their heritage is no small part of the reason their Heavenly brethren pursue them - it's why the Paranoid Descent is archetypically defined by an attempt to find the key to becoming something beyond the grasp of the Machine. They are, in a way, trying to be reborn - and when your most powerful state gives you total access to the backdoors to reality that govern renewal, surely the task of comprehensive personal reinvention is eminently achievable? Along the way, targeted censorship of celestial communiques and the collapse of strategic quantum potentialities at least allows the Inquisitorial Destroyer to make a good showing in matters of covering her tracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T10:34:23-07:00","id":227133,"title":"","content":"Good point, Satchel! I was working on a misconception, for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T19:11:39-08:00","id":317863,"title":"","content":"Upon reflection, the following two make a little more sense as &quot;most-natural fits&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>Messenger/Inquisitor:</b> The Incarnation writeup notes that the Trumpets tend to be a bit paranoid about meaning, information brokers drawing from the same stock as information gatherers-and-disseminators is a sensible basis, Vocal Embeds keying off of communication/revelation/realization and the Agenda Condition's resolution giving information both work on similar logic to An Eye For Disorder and Cacophony Embeds on Destroyers, and the Agenda Condition's Beat criterion suits &quot;agents of change&quot; quite well.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardian/Integrator:</b> Second smallest proportion of example catalysts after Messengers, arguably the least classically demonic type of demon (preservation doesn't resonate quite as much as change, creation, or destruction), most likely to have been assigned to work complementarily with other angels, combination suits the Saboteur/Integrator conflict and the painting of Swords and Shields as &quot;opposite numbers,&quot; the Incarnation's missions suit the tenets of foundational Integrationism, and Instrumental Embeds dealing with timing/precision/utility and material objects suits interaction with the Machine (particularly given the &quot;open question&quot; about Download Knowledge and the fact that Flowers gives the Guardians what technically functions as an angel-summoning Embed). More tenuously, a lot of Defensive Infrastructure being little more than delivery systems for Guardian angels bears some focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2014, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T21:22:58-08:00","id":317936,"title":"","content":"I'm personally a fan of <b>Messenger/Saboteur</b> as a concept. Waging a campaign of psych-war and sig-int against an omnipresent invisible monoculture seems like the perfect fit for a disaffected propagandist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T13:25:18-08:00","id":318461,"title":"","content":"GUARDIAN/TEMPTER: You aren't greedy. Despite what others might assume, you don't really want for much. But your charges have needs, and you need resources for your vigil. So you play their games and you win, but you aren't Greedy! ... At least, that's what you tell yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:25:09-07:00","id":620740,"title":"","content":"Hello! While this thread has been inactive for a while, I figured it might be fun to restart it with some notes on how the Analysts might fit into the Agendas.<br /> <br /> \u2022<b>Analyst/Saboteur:</b> You were designed to look upon the world and see how the Machine might change it. You only saw the pain and destruction it caused, and Fell full or righteous anger. Some of your more aggressive colleagues might accuse you of being passive or even cowardly, but they just don't know how to do things <i>right.</i> Before you act, you gather information, learning everything about anything related to your targets. Though it may take time, when you strike you do so with absolute precision, destroying the forces of the Machine with weaknesses and fracture points they didn't even knew they had.<br /> <br /> \u2022<b>Analyst/Inquisitor:</b> Knowledge is power. Other Inquisitors may believe this adage, but for you it was Mother's Milk. You fellow Paranoids are poseurs compared to you, and you show it with every action. You embody the ideals of your Agenda, studying, analyzing, and destroying information as easily as you breathe. <br /> <br /> \u2022<b>Analyst/Tempter:</b> People want to know. Some will do anything, pay any price, to know some fact or discovery. You play the information trade with deft fingers and eyes, seeking out what others want to know and giving it to them... for a fee, of course. And so Hell will be formed, forged of links of trades and favors, sealed by pay dirt and blackmail.<br /> <br /> \u2022<b>Analyst/Integrator:</b> You used to know everything. You saw all the variables with millions of eyes, understood and sorted data with a mind made of thousands of processors. Now you are deaf, dumb, and blind, struggling to understand a world that's now much bigger seeming than you. Why wouldn't you seek to return to that perfect, potent unity?<br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T15:25:50-07:00","id":621662,"title":"","content":"Well, since others posted Psychopomps working as Tempters and Integrators, I figured I'd try to write short analyses/blurbs for the other 2 Agendas.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopomp/Saboteur:</b> there is no machine so flawless that it can't be taken down with enough understanding and precision. Not even the God-Machine. The Linchpins of Infrastructures are a testament to this truth. Guardians may have an easier time with handling machinery or sensing opportunities for attack with their Instrumental Embeds, sure. But even if you can see bullets coming and send them back by messing around with probability, that won't do you much good if the enemy can do the same. You need to find out what allows them to counter your every move, and you can't do that by kicking down the front door and shooting everyone. You need to be subtle. An intercepted message here, a false lead there. Soon enough, the important bits are exposed for a moment while the enemy looks for something that doesn't exist. Infiltrate and rip it out the Linchpin. Don't forget to have multiple escape routes and a way to erase your trail. Even if they have big guns, they can't kill you if they don't know where you went.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopomp/Inquisitor: </b>what do you think of when you hear the word &quot;Inquisitor&quot;? Someone who sees turncoats everywhere and has ways of making you talk? That might be the case for some of them who prefer dramatic interrogations over efficient ones. The Inquisitors that the Unchained are truly paranoid about are those who don't even need to make their presence known. They just gather whatever they can about you and move co-workers and family away from you, one by one. For the sake of your Cover, you can't just stay here. While you are away, be it in a hospital visit or casino party, they discover your secrets while protecting theirs. No lives lost, no Angels alerted, just unimpeded and perfect movement of all the pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-09-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T17:36:49-07:00","id":623776,"title":"","content":"With the basic blurbs covered, I figured I'd roll over to look at some of the multifaceted combinations.<br /> <br /> <b>Messenger/[Saboteur/Integrator]:</b> Input affects output. That goes beyond Basic and into the realm of Machine Code. You were incarnated to make adjustments to living things, and available evidence indicates that you, your angelic brethren, your demonic comrades, and the Machine that made the lot are all Living Creatures that rely on outside information to direct internal thought processes. Humans are the same way, of course, but you've seen what happens to them when either God or the Unchained gain enough of an edge to go viral, and that prospect terrifies you. So you fudge the numbers on both sides wherever necessary and hope you can cover your tracks well enough for the conflict to reach a quiet resolution before this four-faced free-agency of yours does you in.<br /> <br /> It's tangential, but does the prospect of changing which Embed set Going Loud opens up to be based on Agenda (a la Self-Destruct) rather than Incarnation seem ill-advised to anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:48:32-07:00","id":623886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=623776#post623776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's tangential, but does the prospect of changing which Embed set Going Loud opens up to be based on Agenda (a la Self-Destruct) rather than Incarnation seem ill-advised to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't forsee that ever being a real gamebreaking issue and it solves the &quot;analyst problem&quot; nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T04:03:23-07:00","id":624056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=623776#post623776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's tangential, but does the prospect of changing which Embed set Going Loud opens up to be based on Agenda (a la Self-Destruct) rather than Incarnation seem ill-advised to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's the thing - when you Go Loud, you're not really doing it for getting access to a specific Embed. Embeds, by nature, are necessary subtle powers. Going Loud is anything but subtle. Sure, there might be an exception or three with generally useful powers (why don't you have them already?), but generally speaking, Embeds aren't a big deal in this situation. You want the Primum 10 boost and Exploits.<br /> <br /> There are three big changes in this case. The first is that you are effectively throwing out Incarnations in their entirety. Yes, you have that single Embed or Exploit you have to take at char gen, but its effect is minimal. You're taking something you what for your concept anyways. The second is that it -really- hurts the Uncalled. Not only are you not getting an Agenda bonus, but no affinity Embeds when Going Loud.<br /> <br /> The only ill-advised aspect I can think of is when someone starts joining multiple Agendas. Then, we get affinity for all of the Embeds. But, even then, Embeds aren't that big of a deal. Everyone would possibly want affinity for Cacaphony embeds for the combat utility (its a risk when G.L.), but its not really that big of an issue when we're talking about a 2exp difference between buying the combat Embeds and have them all the time versus buying the 2 dot merit for affinity.<br /> <br /> So, no. Not a big deal at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=623886#post623886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't forsee that ever being a real gamebreaking issue and it solves the &quot;analyst problem&quot; nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not a problem, its a feature. The whole point of playing an Analyst is that you're deliberately breaking the mold from the usual Incarnations. The only defining feature of the Incarnations is the affinity for one of the four kinds of Embeds. If you give an Analyst affinity Embeds, then you're no longer playing an Analyst. Which defeats the whole point of playing an Analyst in the first place. May as well play one of the usual incarnations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T05:28:48-07:00","id":624121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=624056#post624056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not a problem, its a feature. The whole point of playing an Analyst is that you're deliberately breaking the mold from the usual Incarnations. The only defining feature of the Incarnations is the affinity for one of the four kinds of Embeds. If you give an Analyst affinity Embeds, then you're no longer playing an Analyst. Which defeats the whole point of playing an Analyst in the first place. May as well play one of the usual incarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the incarnations as is are barely a step above non-mechanically binding flavour (in so much that it's supposed to inform your character build, but never requires it) I'm not sure that this is a particularly compelling argument against it. As is an Incarnation: forces you to select a single Embed from a category (or have a pre-requisite free Exploit for Analysts) and you get the Embeds from Going Loud. Apart from ideology (which is again, flavour) there are minimal reasons to be tied to a specific incarnation as is. Incarnations could be removed from the game (and you go with the Agendas thing) and it wouldn't fundamentally change how the game plays and how you build characters.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a *bad* thing, mind you. Just they're already basically irrelevant as is and moving it around wouldn't hurt the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:40:15-07:00","id":624314,"title":"","content":"Then why be an Analyst at all? If you walk, talk, and have the abilities of a Destroyer, then you're pretty much a Destroyer. There's simply no reason to include the Analyst as an option if you're just going to make it irrelevant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T08:40:29-07:00","id":624392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=624056#post624056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only ill-advised aspect I can think of is when someone starts joining multiple Agendas. Then, we get affinity for all of the Embeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A la Self-Destruct&quot; means &quot;if you have multiple Agendas you choose which one to filter the effect with when you use it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:33:38-07:00","id":624715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=624314#post624314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why be an Analyst at all? If you walk, talk, and have the abilities of a Destroyer, then you're pretty much a Destroyer. There's simply no reason to include the Analyst as an option if you're just going to make it irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be sidestepping my assertion that the <i>other</i> Incarnations are irrelevant too. They're all basically flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:35:45-07:00","id":624895,"title":"","content":"<b>Destroyer/[Integrator/Saboteur]:</b>In the wake of your Fall, you sought a way to give your purpose meaning again. But you have found it, and everything makes sense now. Both the philosophical circles you run in have many members who espouse that your Maker is the sum of its parts;you have merely take this to its logical conclusion. Your Creator is sick, broken and bloated, gone mad under the weight of its own immense majesty. Your heart has cried out, and you have decided to save it from itself. Some call you a terrorist, a murderer, a madman. You prefer to be called <i>surgeon.</i> And one thing a surgeon understands is that a patient's health is far more important than the patient's whims...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T03:07:10-07:00","id":625271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=624392#post624392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A la Self-Destruct&quot; means &quot;if you have multiple Agendas you choose which one to filter the effect with when you use it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Self-destruct lets you choose which Agenda. While you won't be able to Go Loud and have all Embeds at once... the ability to choose which ones to have active when you do is potentially outstanding. Though, its only <i>potentially </i>a pit fall. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/206801-a-i-overlap-trends-in-the-focuses-of-former-tools-of-the-demiurge?p=624715#post624715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be sidestepping my assertion that the <i>other</i> Incarnations are irrelevant too. They're all basically flavour.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm questioning the point of houseruling a &quot;fix&quot; to something that's both optional and irrelevant. Just don't bother including it in the game. I'm also taking issue with your insinuations that flavor is basically irrelevant - its not. Even if, in game, Incarnation is an artificial construct, its vastly useful as a storytelling tool for Players, Storytellers and characters to use.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}